cting Johnson by 33 votes to 16 for Francis Granger, with 3 not voting.","The Whigs ran regional candidates instead of a single nominee. William Henry Harrison, Hugh Lawson White, Daniel Webster and Willie Person Mangum all won electoral votes as Whigs.","The South Carolina legislature chose the state’s electors, who voted for Willie Person Mangum. Mangum was not on the ballot in any state with a popular vote."],"winner":"vanburen"},"congress":{"number":25,"years":"3/4/1837–3/3/1839","house":{"total":242,"seats":[["Democrats",128],["Whigs",100],["Others",14]],"vacancies":0,"minor":[["Anti-Masonics",7],["Nullifiers",6],["Independent",1]]},"senate":{"total":52,"seats":[["Democrats",35],["Whigs",17]],"vacancies":0}},"sources":[{"title":"Wikipedia, \"1836 United States presidential election\"","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1836_United_States_presidential_election","rev":1385329219},{"title":"House Office of the Historian, \"Party Divisions of the House of Representatives, 1789 to Present\"","url":"https://history.house.gov/Institution/Party-Divisions/Party-Divisions/"},{"title":"Senate Historical Office, \"Party Division\"","url":"https://www.senate.gov/about/parties-leadership/party-division.htm"}]}